  "content": {
    "id": "v2-0-p11-instructions-slot-5-lower-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Use a spreadsheet to answer this question.\n\n$\\$2000$ is invested at the end of each year into an account that pays interest of 4.5% p.a. After how many years will the balance first exceed $\\$30\\,000$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "12 years (balance $\\$30\\,928.06$).",
      "worked": "Set up column A for the number of payments and column B for the balance. Enter 0 in A2 and B2. In B3, enter =B2*1.045+2000. Fill the formula down, retaining full precision.\n\n$$V_0=0,\\qquad V_{n+1}=1.045V_n+2000$$\n\nThe balances to the nearest cent are $V_{11}=\\$27\\,682.36$ and $V_{12}=\\$30\\,928.06$. The balance first exceeds $\\$30\\,000$ after 12 years.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
